        <tr>
            <td>TC-02</td>
            <td>Room Allocation</td>
            <td>Apply for a room when already allocated.</td>
            <td>Application button hidden or error prompts user already has a room.</td>
            <td>Pass</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>TC-03</td>
            <td>Dynamic Billing</td>
            <td>Set monthly expenditure to 10000 with 10 total days attended globally. Assign 5 days to Student A.</td>
            <td>System calculates per-day cost as 1000. Student A's calculated bill is 5000.</td>
            <td>Pass</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>TC-04</td>
            <td>Security & Session</td>
            <td>Attempt to directly navigate to '/home.php' via URL without login track.</td>
            <td>System redirects user forcefully back to the 'index.php' index login page.</td>
            <td>Pass</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>TC-05</td>
            <td>Messaging</td>
            <td>Student sends a grievance regarding water supply.</td>
            <td>Managers dashboard notification bubble updates, message appears in Inbox.</td>
            <td>Pass</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h2>15. Conclusion</h2>
    <p>The Hostel Management System effectively resolves the chaotic constraints of manual hostel administration. By systematically separating administrative powers and student features, it develops an intuitive ecosystem. The implementation of dynamic billing solves a critical financial pain-point, ensuring students only pay for the exact resources they utilize. Overall, H-Track introduces speed, accountability, transparency, and data security to the resident institution.</p>

    <h2>16. Future Scope</h2>
    <p>While the current system covers the essential pillars of hostel management, future expansions could vastly increase its autonomous capabilities:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Online Payment Gateways:</strong> Integration with Razorpay or Stripe to allow students to physically pay dues via credit card/UPI entirely within the app, instead of conceptualizing payments.</li>
        <li><strong>Biometric Attendance Integration:</strong> Connecting external RFID or Fingerprint scanners directly into the MySQL database to automate the daily attendance tracking mechanism—removing the need for managers to manually tick checkboxes.</li>
        <li><strong>Inventory & Mess Management Tracker:</strong> Adding features to track raw materials in the hostel kitchen, staff payroll, and daily menu publication to students.</li>
        <li><strong>Predictive Analytics:</strong> Utilizing historical data to predict student intake capacity curves and budget requirements for subsequent academic semesters.</li>
    </ul>

